WEBVTT

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.380
My name is Onikura Yukinojyo.

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:12.290
I trained as a warrior monk 
from a young age.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:14.880
I spent my days dedicated to training,

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.090
never having known a woman
 even at my current age,

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:21.250
but I always dreamed of having a family.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:26.520
I wanted to live the quiet life one day, 
once there was no more war in the land.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:32.410
If I had died in battle 
as a warrior monk back then,

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:35.180
that would have been impossible.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:38.310
But now I'm here in this era,

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:41.160
so maybe my dream might come true.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:42.840
I'm sure it will!

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:44.320
Oh-ho?

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:46.310
Then, until that day comes,

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:51.150
I'll protect you all as if 
I have a fresh start on life!

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:25.490
<b>"Evil VS Bushido"</b>

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:45.850
Do it!

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.210
Leave it to me!

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:59.490
Hey! There's still one more, old man!

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:05.380
It's a tiger at the front gate 
and a wolf at the back!

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.410
Doctor! Can we get it moving?!

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:11.800
It's impossible!

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:14.000
We don't have enough time to change the tire!

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:22.410
Tch. Luck's just not on our side!

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:30.310
Adam?!

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:39.680
Adam?

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:41.300
What is he doing?

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:52.920
Run!

00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:58.880
Damn it!

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:14.960
<i>So, this is that water sound
 they talked about?</i>

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:21.590
<i>What an annoying sound!</i>

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:27.160
Mom! Adam is...!

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:34.920
That man...

00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:40.450
This is the end.

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:44.450
Come and get it, you lizard bastards!

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:52.330
With this special pack of C4 explosives...

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:57.310
I'll be coming soon, Brian.

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:20.550
Mommy!

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:50.010
Adam!

00:06:10.630 --> 00:06:11.730
I see.

00:06:12.630 --> 00:06:14.160
So, Adam-dono...

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:16.680
Don't let it get you down, Sensui.

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:19.250
He may have had a foul mouth,

00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:22.860
but he went out with honor in the end.

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:26.650
He was feeling regret

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:29.430
about killing Brian.

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:37.640
I see.

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:41.170
All because I was passed out...

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:44.080
That's not true, Sensui!

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:48.210
Both Brian and Adam longed for peace,

00:06:48.210 --> 00:06:50.070
and they were ready to die fighting for it!

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:52.930
Adam even said to me,

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:57.960
"I'm sure you'll be fine 
with Sensui around."

00:07:03.670 --> 00:07:05.900
Thank you.

00:07:10.170 --> 00:07:11.520
Don't worry about it.

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:17.820
I'm sorry to have troubled you.

00:07:19.930 --> 00:07:21.250
All done.

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:24.330
Y-You have my gratitude!

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:27.990
Oh, you're turning red, old man.

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:32.890
I suppose you monks never 
had any women around.

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:37.650
Maybe you're even falling 
for the girl's mother?

00:07:39.230 --> 00:07:41.360
Shut up, brat!

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:43.100
Ow!

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:45.610
Don't grind into my head!

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:55.280
Oh, I don't want to die 
without ever knowing a woman.

00:07:55.280 --> 00:08:01.410
I heard the monks at Eizan 
brought women in for debauchery.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:03.410
We should have snuck in, too...

00:08:03.410 --> 00:08:08.420
That corruption is why Nobunaga's 
men burned them to the ground.

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:11.980
Though, we don't know women,

00:08:11.980 --> 00:08:15.260
and aren't we being pressured 
by Nobunaga's men, as well?

00:08:18.090 --> 00:08:23.250
Wouldn't you try harder to survive 
if you had someone you loved, too?

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:26.500
No, the opposite.

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:27.420
Hmm?

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:33.450
If there were someone I loved, 
I could die for them.

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:36.130
<i>In the Warring States Era,</i>

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:41.350
<i>there was a sect of Pure Land Buddhists 
known as the "Single-Minded School".</i>

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:45.020
<i>At the time, it was a small army 
with powerful military might</i>

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:48.670
<i>while also a faction of the 
most widely-practiced religion.</i>

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:56.590
<i>As Oda Nobunaga advanced 
his unification of Japan,</i>

00:08:56.590 --> 00:09:00.970
<i>he demanded their leader, Kennyo, 
cease supplying his enemies</i>

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:03.060
<i>and withdraw from Ishiyama Honganji.</i>

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:07.410
<i>That led to the Ishiyama Honganji War.</i>

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:12.960
<i>In October of 1570,</i>

00:09:13.290 --> 00:09:17.990
<i>powerful disciples of the 
Single-Minded School in Ise-Nagashima</i>

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:20.700
<i>overthrew Nagashima Castle.</i>

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:24.000
<i>They were skilled in military tactics</i>

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:29.000
<b><i>Advance to Heaven, 
Retreat to Hell</i></b>

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:29.000
<i>and managed to force Nobunaga 
to withdraw from Nagashima.</i>

00:09:36.520 --> 00:09:38.440
<i>Four years later,</i>

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:41.040
<i>Nobunaga gathered an army of 80,000</i>

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:44.520
<i>and laid to siege to 
Nagashima castle once more.</i>

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:48.170
<i>This time, he changed tactics 
and went after their rations,</i>

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:50.620
<i>forcing them to suffer.</i>

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:53.090
<i>Eventually the disciples of Honganji,</i>

00:09:53.090 --> 00:09:57.110
<i>wrought with starvation, 
offered to surrender.</i>

00:09:57.110 --> 00:09:59.650
<i>But Nobunaga</i>

00:10:00.890 --> 00:10:09.500
<i>mercilessly rained gunfire down upon 
anyone who tried to escape the castle.</i>

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:37.120
<i>The disciples fought back in vain</i>

00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:40.640
<i>and Nobunaga set fire to the castle,</i>

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:44.950
<i>burning it to the ground along 
with the 20,000 civilians inside.</i>

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:52.460
Forget about me and go.

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:55.530
What are you saying, Douzan?!

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:57.460
This isn't like you!

00:10:57.910 --> 00:11:01.540
This is my very soul.

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:04.470
Don't give up now!

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:08.480
I threw my life away once already.

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:15.750
I've killed many men with this spiked club,

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:19.690
but at some point even 
my own life became empty.

00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:25.490
Despite that, I've survived all these years, 
unable to sever such thoughts.

00:11:26.590 --> 00:11:29.550
No matter how many feats of glory I achieve,

00:11:29.550 --> 00:11:31.270
I'm just destined to die in vain.

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:35.900
Yukinojyo.

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:39.370
My years with you were enjoyable.

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:43.340
Yes, they truly were.

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:47.490
I wish I could have seen your wife's face.

00:11:47.490 --> 00:11:50.850
I wish I could see it, too.

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:55.790
Douzan?

00:11:56.790 --> 00:11:58.110
H-Hey.

00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:00.860
Hey! Hey!

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:02.340
Douzan!

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:09.520
Douzan!

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:20.370
<i>If there were someone I loved, 
I could die for them, huh?</i>

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:26.910
At this point I have no choice 
but to risk death to protect myself.

00:12:28.190 --> 00:12:31.220
So, I shall fight to the bitter end,

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:34.290
so I can live on!

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:35.600
Kill him!

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:37.030
Earn your glory!

00:12:37.030 --> 00:12:38.380
Yeah!

00:12:38.380 --> 00:12:41.150
That's right! Come and get it!

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:51.620
Hmph, you aren't claiming 
my head that easily!

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:59.080
There he is! This way!

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:22.200
Wh-What?!

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:39.480
D-Douzan!

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:46.890
Where is he?

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:48.020
He's not here.

00:13:48.920 --> 00:13:53.420
Even though I've never been with a woman,

00:13:53.420 --> 00:13:58.920
at my age it wouldn't be strange for me 
to have a child around Kathleen's age.

00:13:58.920 --> 00:14:03.020
Hey, man, don't tell me you like kids 
with that face of yours.

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:04.850
Is that so bad?

00:14:06.940 --> 00:14:08.280
I get it now!

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:11.920
That's why you seem 
so worried about Kathleen.

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:15.040
Well, it's a bit of fatherly affection.

00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:20.820
Why don't you get hitched to the mother, then?

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:22.500
Huh?

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:25.420
Huh?!

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:30.090
Then you'll happily get 
both a wife and a kid at once!

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:31.480
Ow!

00:14:32.280 --> 00:14:33.870
Don't be foolish!

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:36.670
That's just rude to Yurika-dono!

00:14:36.670 --> 00:14:40.470
For one thing, I'm not a kid anymore!

00:14:40.470 --> 00:14:42.300
Ow!

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:45.280
Don't grind into my head!

00:14:56.320 --> 00:14:58.870
Hey guys, look at that.

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:07.460
Like moths to the flame.

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:15.890
Let's take a little break.

00:15:33.220 --> 00:15:34.660
Wh-What is this?!

00:15:55.580 --> 00:15:56.930
What's this?

00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:03.390
No hard feelings against you guys,

00:16:03.810 --> 00:16:06.000
but this is what the world's become.

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:10.440
If you do as we say, we won't harm you.

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:14.950
We're escaped convicts.

00:16:15.390 --> 00:16:17.760
You can call us the Galients.

00:16:18.600 --> 00:16:23.240
Just behave and leave 
your food behind for us.

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:26.030
How deplorable.

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:30.920
Even in this era, there are 
people oppressing other people?

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:35.350
Kanzaki Sensui stands before you!

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:38.680
Oh? You want to go at it?

00:16:39.110 --> 00:16:42.390
Sensui's a real samurai, you know!

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:44.440
He'll win for sure!

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:47.060
A real samurai?

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:52.230
Well, I guess anything could 
happen in this world now.

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:55.450
To think, though, 
that I'd actually get the chance

00:16:55.450 --> 00:16:58.220
to cross swords with a samurai in my life!

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:01.620
You can do it, boss!

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:04.120
<i>He's strong.</i>

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:06.910
Interesting.

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:10.330
None of you interfere!

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:13.210
Hatonami Renjiro.

00:17:13.210 --> 00:17:14.820
Ready!

00:17:15.290 --> 00:17:17.330
Here I come!

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:22.080
He doesn't know his place.

00:17:26.180 --> 00:17:29.080
Show me what you can do!

00:17:36.080 --> 00:17:36.880
No way!

00:17:36.880 --> 00:17:37.730
Boss!

00:17:44.230 --> 00:17:45.650
I used the blunt side.

00:17:46.720 --> 00:17:47.870
Kill me!

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:53.190
My sword is no longer meant 
to cut people down.

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:54.630
Hmm?

00:17:56.930 --> 00:17:58.540
<i>A samurai...</i>

00:17:58.540 --> 00:18:01.470
<i>I want to see how much he's capable of.</i>

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:03.540
Don't do it.

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:06.000
The boss comes first right now.

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:11.060
Come on, Boss.

00:18:12.370 --> 00:18:14.600
Damn it! Fall back for now!

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:18.990
Wh-What?!

00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:26.040
They left?

00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:55.070
What's wrong?

00:18:55.590 --> 00:18:57.320
This tunnel...

00:18:58.460 --> 00:19:00.820
I can't see light from the other side.

00:19:01.590 --> 00:19:06.150
I wouldn't be surprised if there are 
lots of Gibia in this darkness.

00:19:07.740 --> 00:19:11.070
If we get attacked by Gibia in there...

00:19:11.070 --> 00:19:13.330
We won't stand a chance, huh?

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:16.960
But we have to take this road, don't we?

00:19:17.750 --> 00:19:19.810
We can't avoid passing through here.

00:19:20.190 --> 00:19:23.600
I'll cut them down, then.

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:25.420
Please do.

00:19:29.340 --> 00:19:33.270
<i>Sensui? Why is he covering his eye?</i>

00:19:55.740 --> 00:19:56.790
You okay?

00:19:59.680 --> 00:20:02.310
The exit's completely blocked off.

00:20:06.310 --> 00:20:08.310
We're out of options.

00:20:14.910 --> 00:20:17.700
Kenroku, Yukinojyo, we're heading out.

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:18.760
Yeah!

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:20.410
Understood!

00:20:20.410 --> 00:20:21.570
Me, too!

00:20:26.230 --> 00:20:28.550
You stay with Yurika-dono.

00:20:28.550 --> 00:20:30.330
B-But!

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:33.580
Protect your mother.

00:20:38.240 --> 00:20:39.350
All right.

00:20:42.610 --> 00:20:44.840
Everyone, stay safe.

00:20:47.400 --> 00:20:48.790
Hey, Sensui!

00:20:48.790 --> 00:20:50.850
You want front or back?!

00:20:50.850 --> 00:20:52.120
Front!

00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:56.850
Out of my way, insects!

00:21:04.030 --> 00:21:05.890
This is disgusting!

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:14.620
<i>He chose the side with 
the stronger enemies, didn't he?</i>

00:21:20.480 --> 00:21:21.380
In that case!

00:21:42.140 --> 00:21:43.700
<i>At this rate...</i>

00:21:47.870 --> 00:21:48.930
Doctor?

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:55.160
We need to destroy that barricade 
and make a way through.

00:21:56.540 --> 00:21:58.970
We should be able to 
with these hand grenades.

00:22:01.390 --> 00:22:04.880
<i>If we secure our exit quickly, 
everyone will be safe.</i>

00:22:05.290 --> 00:22:06.620
I'll go do it!

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:07.680
Hold on!

00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:12.180
Have a safe trip, Kathleen.

00:22:13.920 --> 00:22:16.450
Yeah, I'll be back in no time.

00:22:28.430 --> 00:22:29.610
There!

00:22:35.870 --> 00:22:37.180
I did it!

00:22:37.660 --> 00:22:38.870
Yes!

00:22:43.180 --> 00:22:44.280
Ow.

00:22:56.860 --> 00:22:59.470
<i>I'm so sorry, everyone!</i>

00:23:00.310 --> 00:23:02.300
Kathleen!

00:23:07.440 --> 00:23:09.780
<b>"Desperate Situation"</b>
